From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 07:49:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rpcrt4: Wait on a copy of a server thread's handle in
 RpcMgmtWaitServerListen().

RpcMgmtWaitServerListen() took protseq->server_thread and waited on it
after leaving listen_cs, while the server thread closes that handle
itself when it ends, under listen_cs.  The waiter could wait on a closed
handle, or on whatever object the handle value had been given to since,
and never return.  CrossOver moved the closing to the waiter, which
leaks the handle of a thread nobody waits for and leaves server_thread
set after the thread is gone; a duplicate taken under the lock keeps the
thread's own bookkeeping as it is.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/dlls/rpcrt4/rpc_server.c b/dlls/rpcrt4/rpc_server.c
index eb733f69980..ddc5ca7f3e7 100644
--- a/dlls/rpcrt4/rpc_server.c
+++ b/dlls/rpcrt4/rpc_server.c
@@ -1569,8 +1569,12 @@ RPC_STATUS WINAPI RpcMgmtWaitServerListen( void )
       EnterCriticalSection(&server_cs);
       LIST_FOR_EACH_ENTRY(protseq, &protseqs, RpcServerProtseq, entry)
       {
-          if ((wait_thread = protseq->server_thread))
+          /* the thread closes its own handle when it ends, under listen_cs: wait on a copy */
+          if (protseq->server_thread &&
+              DuplicateHandle(GetCurrentProcess(), protseq->server_thread, GetCurrentProcess(),
+                              &wait_thread, SYNCHRONIZE, FALSE, 0))
               break;
+          wait_thread = NULL;
       }
       LeaveCriticalSection(&server_cs);
       if (!wait_thread)
@@ -1579,6 +1583,7 @@ RPC_STATUS WINAPI RpcMgmtWaitServerListen( void )
       TRACE("waiting for thread %lu\n", GetThreadId(wait_thread));
       LeaveCriticalSection(&listen_cs);
       WaitForSingleObject(wait_thread, INFINITE);
+      CloseHandle(wait_thread);
       EnterCriticalSection(&listen_cs);
   }
   if (listen_done_event == event)
